Package: libdagda0.3.3
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: distributed object store for a cluster of trusted machines
 Dagda is the store: content-addressed objects held on several nodes with
 evidence of where each copy is, claims and collection, leases, domains with
 their own keys, and the heads that name what a system has written. It is a
 hosted system on Dannan, the network layer.
 .
 This package holds the shared library. Each release is its own package,
 since no release promises another's ABI yet.

Package: libdagda-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Section: libdevel
Depends:
 libdagda0.3.3 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libdannan-dev (>= 0.9.2),
 libdannan-dev (<< 0.10~),
 ${misc:Depends},
Suggests:
 libgtest-dev,
Description: distributed object store for a cluster of trusted machines (development files)
 Dagda is the store: content-addressed objects held on several nodes with
 evidence of where each copy is, claims and collection, leases, domains with
 their own keys, and the heads that name what a system has written.
 .
 This package holds the headers and the CMake package configuration:
 find_package(dagda CONFIG), then link dagda::dagda, which brings Dannan.
 It also holds the in-process cluster test fixture, dagda::test_fixtures,
 header-only, for a hosted system's multi-node tests under GoogleTest.

Package: dagda-tools
Architecture: any
Section: admin
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: distributed object store for a cluster of trusted machines (operator tools)
 Dagda is the store: content-addressed objects held on several nodes with
 evidence of where each copy is, claims and collection, leases, domains with
 their own keys, and the heads that name what a system has written.
 .
 This package holds dagda-migrate, which moves a Macha node's layout v18
 state and disks to Dagda's layout v19 in place, and proves the data survived.
